    description: "SETTLED 2026-09-14, on the third answer in three days. The tiebreaker is the sheet, not the message: `Codex/Tyranids 1.06.ods` -> Armory closes each of its three tables with its own footnote - row 18 \"Point costs are paid per unit.\" under BASIC BIOMORPHS, row 33 \"Point costs are paid per model.\" under ADVANCED, row 47 the same under SPECIAL. The author's worked example reproduces off those rows exactly, which is what made it safe to act on rather than ask a fourth time: a 30-model Gargoyle Brood (a Basic Bioform, per its own KEYWORDS row) pays Pathogenesis 5 for the unit, Infrasonic Roar at the Basic-Bioform price of 1 x 30 = 30, and Endless at the datasheet's own +5 x 30 = 150. The app now charges all three. WHAT PER MODEL MEANS, because the three attempts got it wrong in three different directions: it is the PRICE that scales, not the number of models - every biomorph is bought 0 or 1 times for the whole unit. Attempt one put `per_model` on the GROUP, which charged points x size but also moved the Basic half, which is flat. Attempt two removed it from all 390 Advanced choices on the report that only Living Battering Ram was per model, which undercharged every Advanced biomorph. Attempt three turned the choice-level flag into a STEPPER running up to the model count: Rigzar's screenshot shows a Gargoyle Brood holding FOURTEEN Acid Bloods, with the validator raising an error and letting the purchase through anyway. NOW: `Choice.per_model` multiplies the price by `item.size` exactly like the group flag (points.ts), and the per-choice cap is 1 everywhere (UnitCard.tsx, validators.ts), so the stepper stops at 1 and there is nothing left for the validator to object to. 429 Advanced choices across 39 datasheets carry the flag and the 273 Basic ones do not, checked in both directions by script. LIVING BATTERING RAM is an ordinary Advanced biomorph in all of this - the author: \"per model, yes, but it is supposed to give the weapon to every model in the unit\", which is what its `grants_weapons` entry on the unit already did. The Monstrous-Creature gate from the day before stands (Armory row 26). THE LESSON, and it is the same one as the weapon audit on the same day: three messages produced three different models, and the sheet produced one. Read the table and its footnote before acting on the sentence describing it."
