    description: "2026-09-14. Rigzar: the league was approved and tested, works, so the alpha gate comes off. A read of the module before opening it found three things, two of which were harmless while it was admin-only and are not once players can reach it. (1) A PRIVATE EVENT WAS ONLY PRIVATE ON ONE ENDPOINT. `get` checked visibility; `players`, `games`, `standings` and `export` did not, so any signed-in user who tried an event id could read a private league's participant list with army names and factions, its games, its standings, and download its whole `.json` backup. Test events leaked the same way, which the module is careful about everywhere else. The rule is now one `canReadEvent` helper used by all five. (2) THE REPORTER CHOSE THE OPPONENT'S ARMY. `report-game` accepted `opponentRosterId` from the request and inserted it unchecked ' any roster id, including a third party's list, would then show on the game row, in the standings and on the printed sheet. The UI never sent it; the endpoint accepted it anyway. The field is gone: the opponent's army comes from their own registration. (3) NEW EVENTS DEFAULTED TO TEST DATA. Correct while the module was admin-only and exactly wrong at opening ' the first real league anyone made would have been invisible to everyone but admins. Off by default, and the checkbox is admin-only. ALSO: creating an event is restricted to the senior admins (`is_admin` OR `is_interrogator`) server-side, not just by hiding the button ' Rigzar: \"por ahora solo las ligas las crean los 3 admin principales\". The destructive test tools (seed puppets, reset) stay with `is_admin` alone, since an Interrogator needs to start a league, not to delete data. STILL TRUE, and worth keeping in mind: any test events and puppets made during the alpha should be cleared with Reset before real leagues start, or they will sit in the admins’ own view for ever."
