    description: "FIXED 2026-09-13, reported by Rigzar: \"las cosas de la liga solo estan en ingles, deberian estar en el idioma de la persona\". The module was written straight through in English ' every label, button, tab, form field, placeholder, tag and confirmation ' while the rest of the app has had EN/DE/ES since v1.10. 152 keys added in all three languages and substituted across EventsModal and LeagueSheet. THE HALF THAT WOULD HAVE BEEN EASY TO MISS is the server: a refusal like \"This league is closed\" or \"That army is 4000 points and this event is capped at 2500\" is composed in `api/events/[action].js`, so translating the components alone would have left every error message in English. `bad()` now takes an optional translation KEY and `vars`, the client looks the key up in the reader's language and fills the template, and the English text is always sent alongside so an unknown or missing key degrades to readable English rather than to nothing ' which is also what a stale client looks like after a deploy. Only the refusals a PLAYER can hit carry a key; admin-only plumbing errors deliberately do not, because they are read by three people who all read English and a badly translated operational message is worse than an untranslated one. TWO THINGS STAY IN THE LANGUAGE THEY WERE WRITTEN IN, on purpose: an organiser's league name and description, and the note a player types when disputing a game. Those are their words. Machine-translating user prose is a separate question and is NOT done here ' see the battle-report entry."
