    title: "Imperial Guard \u2014 Ministorum World MUST take a third Trait, but Skirmish now allows only one (rules contradiction)",
    description: "NOT A BUG, a contradiction between two canonical documents, found while verifying the new Skirmish Trait cap in the running app rather than from a report. The Missions supplement's September 2026 revision adds \"Only one Trait may be selected.\" to the Skirmish restrictions. `Codex/Imperial Guard`, Army Customisation, Ministorum World Legacy, says \"The army must select a third Trait.\" — not may, MUST. Skirmish does not forbid Legacies (it forbids Archetypes and allies), so an Imperial Guard army can legally take Ministorum World in a Skirmish game and then be told by its own Legacy to take three Traits and by the engagement to take one. HOW THE APP RESOLVES IT, and why: the engagement cap wins. That matches how every other Skirmish restriction already behaves — the same list forbids Archetypes outright and zeroes every free-slot mechanic in the game with \"All units occupy an Army Organisation slot, even if their rules state otherwise\", so the supplement plainly expects to override datasheet and Customisation text at that game size. A Skirmish list with Ministorum World therefore gets one Trait slot, and the Legacy's third-Trait sentence simply cannot be honoured. SCOPE, checked rather than assumed: Ministorum World is the ONLY entry in the entire game that MANDATES an extra Trait (`trait_slot_bonus` appears exactly once across all 21 archetypes files). Dark Eldar's Coordinated Raid grants a bonus Trait slot too, but it is an Archetype, and Archetypes are already illegal in Skirmish — so this is the only collision that exists. PUT TO THE AUTHOR: should Ministorum World be unavailable in Skirmish, or should its third Trait override the engagement cap? Either answer is a one-line change; guessing is not. Until then the app does the conservative thing and nothing is silently granted. RESOLVED THE SAME EVENING, and there was never a contradiction to resolve — the author's own changelog says \"Ministorum World legacy now grants the third Trait for free\", and codex 1.05 rewrites the entry to \"The army must select two Traits and may then select a third Trait that is paid per unit (not per model). That Trait is free.\" MAY, not must. So the Skirmish cap simply means the extra slot goes unused at that game size, and nothing collides. Our copy was carrying the OLD wording, which is where the contradiction came from. Now implemented as written: the third pick costs 0 points for every unit (store), and because the sentence restricts WHICH Trait may fill that slot — one paid per unit, not one marked with the asterisk that means per Wound or Hull point — a per-model Trait in the third slot is an error. That check matters precisely because the slot is free either way: without it a player would get an illegal Trait at no cost and never be told.",
