    status: "fixed",
    title: "Tyranids \u2014 a Warrior swapping Spinefists for a Barbed strangler or Venom cannon kept both (GH#116)",
    description: "FIXED 2026-09-11 (v1.71), reported via the in-app form (GitHub #116: \"Barbed Strangler/Venom Cannon swaps for Tyranid Warriors do not replace spinefists for either the live profile or regular weapon swap\"). CONFIRMED against `Codex/Tyranids 1.05.ods` (full sheet read): the option is \"For every three models, one Tyranid Warrior may swap their Spinefists\", and production's option group carried no `replaces`, so the chosen gun was added alongside the Spinefists rather than instead of them. The SAME datasheet's other Spinefist swap (Scything talons / Devourer / Deathspitter) already had `replaces` correctly, which is why only the heavy-weapon option misbehaved. Fixed by adding `replaces: [\\\"Spinefists\\\"]`. VERIFIED: a three-model brood taking one Barbed strangler now resolves to 1x Barbed strangler + 2x Spinefists; before the fix the Spinefists row was unchanged. NOTE ON THE SWEEP THIS PROMPTED, because it is worth not repeating: a first probe reported this very unit as FINE. It compared weapon counts before and after, and on this datasheet the count is null on both sides, so the comparison fell through to a pass. A second probe then over-corrected and flagged 27 groups by treating \"weapon still listed\" as failure — which is normal and correct whenever only some models in a squad swap. Neither number is trustworthy, so nothing was mass-edited: only the reported datasheet was fixed, on evidence I read directly. THAT AUDIT IS NOW DONE (same day): all 27 candidate groups were checked one at a time. Method, after two bad probes: apply the proposed `replaces` IN MEMORY, resolve the unit before and after, and compare the swapped weapon's count — no guessing from sentence shape. 26 changed the result correctly and the 27th (Termagant Brood) looked like a no-op until tested as the CHAINED swap it is (Spinefists — Fleshborer — Strangleweb): with all ten Termagants on Fleshborers and one swapping again, the card read 10 Fleshborers AND 1 Strangleweb, eleven weapons for ten models. All 27 fixed. FIVE HEADER SHAPES were spot-checked verbatim against their .ods first (\"for every N, one may swap\", \"up to two may replace\", \"all remaining models\", a single-model \"can exchange its X\", and \"one pair of\"), and ONE header needed a hand correction the automatic rule got wrong: Inquisition Servitors read \"swap their Paired shock chargers FOR A Shock charger and...\" — the Shock charger is what you receive, so only the pair is given up. THE EVIDENCE THAT THESE WERE OMISSIONS, NOT DESIGN: the Ork Boyz datasheet carries TWO \"swap their Choppa and Slugga\" groups, identically worded, one with `replaces` and one without — exactly like the reported Tyranid Warriors. Verified after: zero candidates remain, and `sanity_sweep` went from 132 findings to 131, so nothing new was introduced. New permanent guard `scripts/check_weapon_swaps.ts` fails the build-time check if a swap group ever loses its `replaces` again.",
