    id: "ki-quoted-ability-negated-shown-as-granted-01",
    status: "fixed",
    title: "Vehicle cards listed the damage results their wargear protects against as abilities they had (19 items, 14 factions)",
    description: "FIXED 2026-09-11 (v1.71), reported on Discord with a screenshot of a Leman Russ Tank Commander whose Abilities column read \"Crew Shaken\" and \"Engine damage\" — two VEHICLE DAMAGE RESULTS, listed as though the tank possessed them. CommissarWoods called the cause correctly in the thread: \"i think when you add extra armour\". CAUSE: `parseEquipMods` harvests quoted names out of an item's description and adds them to the granted-abilities list, with no notion of whether the sentence is granting or denying. Additional armor is \"The model ignores the first 'Crew Shaken' vehicle damage each round\" and Chain guard is \"The model ignores 'Engine damage' vehicle damage on a roll of 4+\", so both had their quoted term advertised as a possessed ability — precisely inverting what the wargear does. SWEPT the whole game rather than patching the two reported: 19 items in 14 factions have this shape, essentially every faction's Additional armor (Adeptus Mechanicus, Custodes, Sororitas, Grey Knights, Inquisition, Necrons, Orks, Dark Eldar, Genestealer Cults, Imperial Guard) plus its differently-named equivalents: Eldar and Harlequin \"Spirit stones\", Tau \"Decoy launchers\", Votann \"Additional void armor\" and the IG \"Chain guard\". FIX: before the quoted names are collected, the description is scanned for negating verbs (ignores / immune to / cannot suffer / does not suffer / is not affected by / never suffers / prevents) and any quoted term reached from one WITHIN THE SAME CLAUSE (no full stop or semicolon between) is excluded. Clause-scoped on purpose so a later sentence that genuinely grants something is untouched. VERIFIED both ways: the reported Tank Commander with Additional armor and a Chain guard now shows only its three real abilities (Move through cover, Lumbering Behemoth, Officer), and items that genuinely grant a quoted ability still do — CSM Terrain expert keeps Move through cover and Use cover, the Space Marine bike keeps Devastating Charge.",
