    description: "FIXED 2026-09-11 (v1.71), reported via the in-app form (GitHub #119: \"Jetbike does not add twin shuriken catapult to live profile\", Eldar). SAME CLASS AS GH#112, which I had already swept — and this one got through that sweep, so the detector was rebuilt rather than the item patched. The old check matched SENTENCE SHAPES (`isGrantWeapon`: \"the model gains a X\" where X ends in gun/cannon/missile/weapon). The new one cross-references item descriptions against the faction's REAL weapon names, which does not care how the sentence is built. It found 13 items in 9 factions granting nothing: Eldar + Harlequins \"Eldar jetbike\" (twin shuriken catapult), Votann Skimmer bike, HH Legion Scimitar Jetbike, CSM Doombike, Chaos Daemons Screamer of Tzeentch, GK Warden of the Blade, Necrons Staff of the Destroyer, IG Twin heavy stubber, Tau Knarloc steed / Markerlight / XV84. Three distinct reasons they slipped: compound sentences, \"it gains\" instead of \"the model gains\", and names ending in an unlisted word (\"stubber\"). SECOND PROBLEM FOUND WHILE FIXING: `effect.grants_weapons` is resolved ONLY against `armory_general.weapons`, so naming a weapon that is not in that list grants nothing silently — six of the thirteen needed the weapon added there first, as granted-only entries (both prices null, the \"Ossific Blades\" convention). VERIFIED by buying each item on a real unit of its faction and confirming the weapon appears on the resolved card: 11 of 12 testable cases pass (the twelfth is the Krootox steed name collision, its own issue). Baseline check: `sanity_sweep` reports 132 findings both before and after, so nothing new was introduced. New permanent guard: `scripts/check_weapon_grants.ts`, which also flags a `grants_weapons` naming a weapon missing from the armoury list. It now reports 3 items, all reviewed and all genuine false positives (Sororitas Holy promethium, Tau Tactical philosophies, Ork Nitro Squigs — each MENTIONS a weapon in order to BOOST it, not to grant it).",
