    description: "FOUND 2026-09-11 while fixing GH#119, and NOT fixable as data. `Codex/Tau Empire ENG.ods` has TWO separate Armory rows both named \"Krootox steed\": one reading \"+6\\\" Movement, +2 Strength, +2 Toughness, +2 Wounds, a 5+ Save and the \\\"Bike\\\" ability. Only for Kroot Shapers.\" and another reading \"+2 Strength, +2 Toughness, +2 Wounds, a 5+ Save, a Krootox fist, and changes its unit type to \\\"Monstrous Infantry\\\". Kroot infantry only.\" Different text, different targets, different prices. The app looks an armoury purchase up by NAME (`findArmoryItem`), so it always resolves to the first one: whichever the player clicks, they get the Kroot Shaper version's effects and price. The Krootox fist grant added in v1.71 is correct for the second entry but can never fire while the collision stands. Fixing this properly means either renaming an entry (which breaks saved lists, since a selection stores its item NAME) or teaching selections to carry a disambiguator — neither is a data edit, and the duplicate name is in the canonical sheet, so it is a question for the author first. ALSO UNRESOLVED, same batch: the Tau XV81 Crisis battlesuit grants \"a Smart missile system\", but the codex prints TWO different profiles under that exact name — Support Turrets and Broadside get 30\\\" Heavy 3 S5 AP0 with Indirect and Sunder(2), while Hammerhead, Devilfish, Sky Ray and Riptide get AP-1 with Seeking. The battlesuits themselves disagree, so there is no defensible way to pick one for the XV81. FIXED BY THE CODEX ITSELF, 2026-09-12 — both halves, and neither needed a judgement call. The author renamed the first \"Krootox steed\" entry to \"Kalamandra steed\", so the two armoury rows no longer collide; every saved selection is mapped forward through RENAMED_ARMORY_ITEMS, which matters because lookup returns the FIRST match — without the mapping each owner would silently have ended up with the OTHER item. And the September sheet brings all three \"Smart missile system\" profiles into line: Support Turrets, Hammerhead and Devilfish now all print 30\" Heavy 3 S5 AP-1 D1 Anti-Air, Seeking (the turret's used to be AP 0 with Indirect and Sunder(2)), so there is nothing left to choose between. WHICH EXPOSED A THIRD PROBLEM NOBODY HAD SEEN: with the ambiguity gone the XV81 still granted nothing, because the weapon-grant text parser read \"The model gains a Smart missile system\" as granting \"Smart missile\" — a name no armoury contains — and the resolver only resolves grants against armory_general.weapons. The item is now wired explicitly (effect.grants_weapons) with the profile added to the Tau armoury as a granted-only row. Tightening scripts/check_weapon_grants.ts to verify the parsed name actually resolves immediately found FOUR MORE of the same shape: the Hunter-killer missile equipment in Space Marines, Imperial Guard, Adeptus Custodes and Adeptus Sororitas, all sold at 5 points on vehicles, none of which had the weapon's 120\" Heavy 1 S8 AP-3 D2 Ammo(1), AT(2) profile in their armoury — while Chaos Space Marines, Grey Knights and Inquisition, which sell the same item, did. All four fixed from their own sheets.",
