    status: "fixed",
    title: "Imperial Guard \u2014 a targeted weapon enhancement only reached one firing mode of a multi-profile weapon (GH#115)",
    description: "FIXED 2026-09-10, reported via the in-app bug form (GitHub #115: \"Regimental artefact doesn't update weapon stats when applied to vehicles\", Imperial Guard Leman Russ Tank Commander). NOT a repeat of GH#109/#110 — the weapon-target picker added then works fine. Reproduced headlessly across the realistic builds before changing anything: all four enhancements (+6\\\" Range / +1 Strength / -1 AP / +1 AT) applied correctly to the default weapons AND to an option-chosen main gun. The failing case is a weapon with MULTIPLE FIRING MODES. `availableWeapons` in ArmoryModal was built from `unit.weapons.map(w => w.name)`, which is one entry per mode, so a tank with plasma cannon sponsons offered \"Plasma cannon (Standard)\" and \"Plasma cannon (Overheating)\" as two separate targets; the resolver then matched `b.targetWeapon === w.name` exactly, so the bonus landed on that one profile and the sibling kept its original numbers. Picking \"(Standard)\" and then firing overcharged shows no change at all, which is exactly what was reported. FIX, three parts: the numeric boost matcher and the ability-grant path in `resolver.ts` both work by BASE name now, so an enhancement covers every profile of the weapon it was bought for; and the dropdown dedupes by base name so each weapon is offered once. Lists saved with a profile name still resolve, because the matcher normalises both sides. VERIFIED: with sponson plasma cannons, all four enhancements now change both profiles whether the stored target is \"Plasma cannon\" or \"Plasma cannon (Standard)\", and +1 AT reaches both. FOUND WHILE HERE and fixed in the same pass: `weaponsToShow` never receives these boosts (they are applied when `weaponGroups` is built), and the Tabletop Simulator export was reading that list — so TTS cards showed unmodified profiles and dropped granted abilities entirely. It now builds from `weaponGroups` and merges each group's traitMap, matching the unit card.",
