    status: "fixed",
    title: "Eldar Exarch Powers (Bladestorm, Crack shot, ...) had no mechanical effect defined ANYWHERE — not even for a unit's own native purchase, let alone Paragon of war",
    description: "FIXED 2026-08-29. FOUND the same day while fixing the general \"an Armory item's effect never reached the chosen weapon\" bug and auditing every named-choice picker for the same gap (Crusade weapon's 5 enhancements were fixed the same pass — see ki-hh-crusade-weapon-no-enhancement-picker-01/the changelog). Eldar's \"Paragon of war\" (Armory item, \"can choose a single Exarch power\") already had a working `chosenPower` picker, but unlike Crusade weapon's 5 self-contained enhancements, the 16 named Exarch Powers (Bladestorm, Burning heat, Crack shot, Crushing blows, Defensive stance, Dragon's bite, Graceful avoidance, Heartstrike, Lightning attacks, Piercing strike, Rapid redeployment, Reaper's reach, Scorpion's sting, Skyhunter, Stand firm, Surprise assault) appear as bare `{ name, points }` choices with NO `effect` field, both in Paragon of war's own picker AND in the option_groups of the 10 Aspect Warrior units that grant them natively (Dire Avengers, Fire Dragons, Howling Banshees, Shadow Spectres, Striking Scorpions, Shining Spears, Swooping Hawks, Warp Spiders, Crimson Hunter, Dark Reapers) — so they had NEVER had a mechanical effect in this engine, for ANY purchase path. Read the Eldar .ods's own \"EXARCH POWERS\" armoury section for the canonical text of all 16 and built `EXARCH_POWER_EFFECTS` (equipMods.ts): each power grants either a `unitAbility` (e.g. Bladestorm → \"Shuriken\", Stand firm → \"Objective secured!\") or an `allWeapons` effect scoped to melee or ranged (a named ability, a Deadly-stacking step-up, an AT step-up, or Reaper's reach's flat +6\" range on every ranged weapon). Wired into `resolver.ts` via a new `getActiveExarchPowers(unit, item)` helper that collects the chosen power name from BOTH purchase paths — Paragon of war's `chosenPower` AND a native unit's own selected option-group choice, matched by name since neither carries an `effect` field — so one code path now covers both. While verifying this live, ALSO found and had to undo a self-inflicted regression: an initial `SHARED_PREFIX_STAT_ITEMS` table added to equipMods.ts to fix what looked like a SEPARATE bug (\"Paragon of war\"/\"Paragon of fate\"'s own \"+1 Strength, Toughness, Wounds and Attacks\" text only ever applying Strength) turned out to duplicate a fix that already existed in the production JSON's `effect.stat_mod` for both items (applied via the unrelated `optionStatMods` pipeline) — the two together double-counted T/W/A (an Autarch showed T5/W5/A6 instead of T4/W4/A5, S alone stayed correct). Caught via a temporary debug log proving `equipMods.statDeltas` was always the correct `{S:1,T:1,W:1,A:1}​`, so the extra point had to be coming from elsewhere; removed the redundant table rather than touching the already-correct JSON. Verified live end to end on a fresh build: Eldar Autarch + Paragon of war + Heartstrike shows S4◆/T4‡/W4‡/A5‡ (no doubling); + Reaper's reach moves Plasma grenade's range 6\"→12\"; a native Dire Avenger Exarch (no Paragon of war at all) + Heartstrike shows its Diresword's Deadly(5+) stack to Deadly(4+) — confirming both purchase paths share the same, now-correct code path.",
