    description: "FIXED 2026-08-29, reported in chat (Rigzar: bought Obsidian blade on a Warpsmith, targeted a weapon in the Armory's own \"Apply to\" picker, paid the +20pts — \"no le dio el bono\", the weapon never showed Deadly(5+)). CAUSE: `ArmoryModal.tsx` already had a fully working weapon-target picker (`requiresWeaponTarget()`, the \"Apply to\" dropdown, storing the choice as `sel.targetWeapon` on the purchase) — built and used correctly for one narrow case, daemon weapon traits. `resolver.ts` only ever READ `sel.targetWeapon` for `section === 'daemon_weapons'` selections; for the `equipment` section — where Obsidian blade, Master-crafted weapon, Relic blade, and every other single-weapon-target item actually live — nothing downstream ever consumed the stored choice. The dropdown worked, the points were charged, and the effect was a complete no-op, on every single one of these ~35 items in every faction that has one (grepped the whole game for \"one weapon of the model gains\"/\"on one of its weapons\"/\"purchased for each weapon\"). FIX, two parts: (1) a new `CHOSEN_WEAPON_GRANT_ITEMS` table in `equipMods.ts` (mirroring the existing `NAMED_WEAPON_BOOST_ITEMS`/`RANGED_STRENGTH_BOOST_ITEMS` pattern already used for similar named-item effects) covers the 16 items whose effect isn't a plain quoted ability name — the generic \"may re-roll one to-hit roll per activation\" reroll text used by 10 factions' own \"Master-crafted weapon\" (→ grants the same \"Master-crafted\" ability Space Marines' own entry already quotes explicitly), Obsidian blade/Cegorach's Rose's Deadly-stacking rule (\"if the weapon already has the rule, increase Deadly(x+) by 1\" — a step-up from whatever it already has, not just \"grant 5+ and keep the better value\"), Relic blade/Holy weapon/Cursed blade's +1 Damage, Maelstrom Weapon/Reaver Weapon's +1 Strength, and the Eldar Ynnari/Fire blade relics. (2) `resolver.ts` gained a new pass in `resolveUnitProfile` that reads `sel.targetWeapon` for `equipment`-section selections and injects the effect into that weapon's row — ability grants go through the SAME `weaponTraitMap` mechanism trait-granted weapon abilities already use (so the existing merge-the-better-value logic, e.g. for Deadly, keeps working unmodified), and a new `applyChosenWeaponStatBoosts()` (mirroring `applyNamedWeaponBoosts`) applies the numeric Strength/AP/Damage deltas to the weapon's own stat row. Items worded as an enumerable choice (\"gains one of the following: Range/Strength/AP/AT\") are deliberately excluded — see ki-enumerable-weapon-relic-no-enhancement-picker-01, a separate, bigger gap. Verified live: a Warpsmith's Meltagun tendril gains \"Deadly(5+)\" from Obsidian blade; a Lieutenant's Astartes chainsword gains BOTH \"Master-crafted\" (from Master-crafted weapon) and +1 Damage (from Relic blade, D:1 → D:2) at the same time, correctly.",
