    description: "FIXED 2026-08-26, GitHub #98 (\"Psyker characters cannot take Craftworld Armory items\"). CAUSE: `resolveEldarCharPrice()` in `ArmoryModal.tsx` always reads `arm.p_unit` for a Psyker character buyer and `arm.p_char` for a non-Psyker one — correct for the General Armoury sheet, which genuinely prices Witchblade-style items off two separate \"POINTS PSYKER\"/\"POINTS AUTARCH\" columns (parsed into p_unit/p_char respectively). The Craftworld and Ynnari Armoury sheets are a different shape entirely: a single \"POINTS CHARACTER\" column meant for ANY character, parsed into `p_char` with `p_unit` never even present as a key. A Psyker buyer always read the (nonexistent) p_unit column for these sheets and found nothing. FIX: added a fallback — when the preferred column for the buyer's role is both null AND genuinely absent from the item (`!(key in arm)`, not just falsy), fall back to whichever price actually exists. Key-presence, not just null-checking, is what keeps this safe: a General Armoury item's real \"-\" (Aspect armor is Autarch-only, stored as an explicit `p_unit: null`) still blocks a Psyker, since that key IS present — only a sheet that never had the column at all triggers the fallback. Verified live: a Farseer under the Swordwind Legacy could not buy \"Fate Reader\" before the fix (blocked, \"-\"); after, it shows +15pts and is purchasable (65→80pts). Regression-checked \"Aspect armor\" in the General Armoury stays correctly blocked for the same Farseer (still shows \"-\").",
