    status: "fixed",
    title: "Print View didn't resolve an item bought from a Horus Heresy/Legio Titanicus unit's host-codex \"General\" tab",
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-26 auditing the separate-tabs fix above, not reported by a player; fixed same day per Rigzar (\"primero repara eso de la armeria en el print view\"). CAUSE: `PrintView.tsx` has its own small local `findArmoryItem(data, name, factionSource?)` helper (predates the engine's `armorySource.ts` one, never merged, never updated even during the earlier merge-based fixes) used to look up a bought item's full description for the printed card and the Special Rules section — it only ever searched the item's OWN supplement/ally FactionData, so an item bought from the new \"GENERAL\" (host codex) tab wouldn't resolve there: no description, no stats on the card. Its `factionSource` parameter was already dead code (no call site ever passed a 3rd argument), so no existing behavior depended on it. FIX: repurposed that unused 3rd parameter into `hostData?: FactionData` — a fallback the function recurses into when the item isn't found in `data`'s own armories — and passed the primary `data` (already in scope at all 4 call sites) as that fallback. Verified live: bought \"Bionics\" (a Chaos Space Marines general-armory item, \"The model gains a 6+ ward save.\") on a Legion Tactical Squad from its new GENERAL tab — Print View's Special Rules section now correctly shows \"Bionics: The model gains a 6+ ward save.\"",
