    description: "FOUND AND FIXED 2026-08-26, reported live (Rigzar: a Space Marines Lieutenant/Captain with Terminator armor bought showed \"VETERAN ABILITIES — LIEUTENANT / Terminator armour — showing only Terminator-compatible items (ᵀ). / No items in this section\"). CAUSE: `ArmoryModal.tsx`'s `filterTermCompat`/`filterGravisCompat`/`filterGlyphArmourCompat` (the gates that restrict a Terminator/Cataphractii/Gravis-armoured model's Armory picks to only ᵀ/ᴳ-marked items) ran on EVERY item list including the Veteran Abilities picker (`filterCategory=\"veteran\"`) — but checked against the Space Marines .ods, the \"VETERAN ABILITIES\" table is a wholly separate section that starts right AFTER the ᵀ/ᴳ restriction notes and the WEAPONS/EQUIPMENT table they gate (row 104 vs. the notes at rows 102-103), with its own header/columns, and none of its 8 items (Counter-attack, Favoured enemy, Furious charge, Infiltrator, Outflank, Tank hunter, Terrain expert, Vanguard) carry a ᵀ/ᴳ glyph in their name — unlike genuinely gated equipment (e.g. \"Trophyᴳ ᵀ\"). The restriction is about wargear bulk/fit, not about tactical doctrines a model already knows; a model in Terminator armor still has every Veteran Ability available. Once a player picked \"Terminator armor\" as their one veteran-slot equipment choice, `termRestricted` flipped true and silently hid all 7 remaining plain (non-glyphed) abilities from the SAME picker, with no way to change the pick. FIX: all three gates now pass `category === 'veteran'` items through unconditionally, matching the .ods's own table boundary. Verified live: Lieutenant promoted to Captain, bought Terminator armor from the new host-codex GENERAL tab, reopened Veteran Abilities — all 8 abilities show again (the ᵀ-restriction banner still correctly shows on the Armory's general weapons/equipment tabs, unaffected).",
