    description: "FOUND during the 2026-08-26 HH audit, fixed same day per Rigzar (\"haz esa funcion nueva\"). The .ods reads \"Every model got access to melee weapons from the Armory. May not select weapons with the 'Slow' or 'Unwieldy' rule.\" The engine had `armory_weapons_only`/`armory_gear_only` flags to restrict a unit to just weapons or just equipment, but nothing to further restrict to melee-only weapons, and nothing to exclude items whose ability text names \"Slow\"/\"Unwieldy\" — every model could buy ranged weapons and Slow/Unwieldy melee weapons (Power fist, Thunder hammer, Chainfist, ...) from the host codex's General Armory with no restriction at all. FIX: added a new `armory_melee_only` unit flag (`types/data.ts`), set on Palatine Blade Squad, and a `filterMeleeOnlyNoSlowUnwieldy()` gate in `ArmoryModal.tsx` — scoped to the WEAPONS section only (equipment untouched), keeps already-bought items visible like every other armour/glyph gate, wired into both the actual item list (`getItems()`) and the sub-tab visibility count (`activeTabSectionItems()`). Verified live: the General tab's Weapons list now shows only melee items (Astartes chainsword, Combat knife, Force axe/staff/sword, Lightning claw, Ossific Blades, Power axe/maul/sword) — Power fist, Thunder hammer and Chainfist (all melee but Slow/Unwieldy) and every ranged weapon are correctly absent.",
