    description: "FIXED 2026-08-21 (v1.65), Discord: the Dreadnought's Psyker line reads \"It knows Smite and Fortitude,\" and Woods asked where Fortitude actually was — \"I'm sorry, I'm still not seeing where it should be.\" It genuinely was not anywhere: unlike every other named power, Fortitude is not part of a shared discipline list, it is printed directly on the Dreadnought's own sheet (its own Name/Range/Target/Cast value/Effect/Duration/Complexity block), and identically on Land Raider, Land Raider Crusader, Land Raider Redeemer, Razorback, Rhino and Stormraven Gunship. The psychic-mode parser had no pattern for \"knows Smite and <a single named power>\" — it fell back to 'unlimited' mode, which is doubly wrong: the power was invisible, AND the model could freely browse every other Grey Knights discipline it had no business seeing. NEW: `Unit.fixed_power`, a datasheet-embedded power shown exactly like Smite (an always-known card, not a pick), and a psychic-mode check that clears discipline access to none when the power named in the text matches. Eldar's Spiritseer has the identical construction — \"It knows Smite and Craftsong\" — with Craftsong on its own sheet the same way; fixed with the same field. Verified live: the Dreadnought's Psychic Powers modal now shows Smite and Fortitude both as Always Known, with \"No disciplines available for this unit.\"",
