    status: "fixed",
    title: "\"All ranged weapons of the model gain +1 Strength\" items changed nothing",
    description: "FIXED 2026-08-21 (v1.65, GitHub #92): Psy-ammunition on Grey Knights read \"All ranged weapon of the model gain +1 Strength. Only works on weapons with Strength 4 or below,\" and buying it changed nothing — \"I expected the strength value to be increased to 5.\" CAUSE: the shared equipMods stat-delta parser reads \"+1 Strength\" in an item's description as a bump to the model's own S CHARACTERISTIC, which is invisible on any weapon whose printed Strength is a flat number rather than \"U\" (User's Strength) — true of every weapon on every unit with Psy-ammunition access. The bonus is per-WEAPON, conditioned on that weapon's own printed Strength, not a model-level stat at all. FIX: a new resolver pass raises the Strength of qualifying ranged weapons directly (melee and non-numeric profiles like \"U\"/\"x2\" are left alone), and the equipMods parser's AURA_PHRASES guard was widened from \"one weapon of the model\" to also catch \"all weapon(s) of the model,\" so the false characteristic-level bump no longer fires alongside it. Same fix applied to the three other items with the identical wording, found while auditing this: Inquisition's \"Psybolt ammunition\" (same text, same bug), Tau's \"Overdrive Power Systems\" (Bork'an Sept relic, uncapped — all ranged weapons, no Strength-4 ceiling), and Tyranids' \"Symbiostorm\" (Kronos Hive Fleet legacy, also uncapped). Grey Knights' 7 squads with built-in Psy-ammunition access (Strike/Terminator/Ghost Terminator/Paladin/Purifier/Interceptor/Purgator) needed a second detection path, since they grant it through the unit's own inline option group rather than a general Armory purchase — item.armory never held it for these, only item.optionQty did. Verified live: a Terminator Squad's Storm bolter and Frag grenade (both printed Strength 4) read Strength 5 after buying it; Krak grenade (Strength 6) and the melee Nemesis force weapon are unchanged. NOT FIXED, different shape: Orks' Warbuggy item \"All of this model's Squig Launchas receive +1 Strength and -1 AP\" has the same false-characteristic-bump bug (also now suppressed by the widened AURA_PHRASES) but needs weapon-NAME matching rather than a range-type-and-threshold rule, since it targets one named weapon rather than every ranged weapon under a cap.",
