    description: "FIXED 2026-08-16 (v1.62), found during the first audit of every Armory sheet. Inquisition.ods / Armory prints, under the WEAPON table: \"Acolyte Specialists can only receive weapons marked with ˢ.\" Nine weapons carry the glyph — Bolt pistol, Chainsword, Eviscerator, Frag grenade, Hot-shot laspistol, Krak grenades, Laspistol, Needle pistol, Power stake — and production stripped the glyph from item names, so the restriction existed nowhere and an Acolyte could be handed a Thunder hammer. SCOPE, established from the sheets rather than guessed: a Henchman Warband is built \"from the Elite section\", and of those 18 specialist datasheets the Acolytes are the ONLY one that grants Armory access at all (\"All models got access to weapons and gear from the Armory\") — so the rule can only bite there, which is where the gate is applied. FIX: new optional `ArmoryItem.specialist_compat`, set on exactly those nine weapons (verified: 9 on the sheet, 9 flagged, and no stray flag in any other faction or list), plus a weapons-only filter in ArmoryModal for the Acolytes datasheet. Held as a field rather than as a glyph on the name — the Tau ᴵ approach — because a saved list stores the item's NAME and renaming nine live weapons would orphan every Inquisition list holding one. An already-bought item stays listed, as with every other gate, so no saved list loses gear silently. LIMIT: inside a mixed Henchman Warband the app buys for the unit, not for a named model type, so a Warband containing both Acolytes and Crusaders is not filtered — restricting the whole Warband to nine weapons would be wrong for every other specialist in it. Every other superscript was checked in the same pass and is enforced: ᵀ Terminator and ᴳ Gravis via term_compat/armour_compat, ᴹ Mega armor and ᴱ Exo-armor via the name glyph (engine/keywords.ts GLYPH_ARMOUR_NAMES), ᴵ Tau Infantry via the unit-type filter, the Chaos Marks via the mark armouries, and the Dark Eldar ᴷ/ᶜᵒ/ᶜᵘ via sub-faction.",
