    title: 'Eldar — swapping one of a War Walker\'s two Scatter lasers deleted both',
    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13, GitHub #86, and it was our own regression from v1.59. Fixing GH#81 taught UnitCard that a group worded "may swap EACH <weapon>" offers one swap per copy carried, so a War Walker could finally swap both of its Scatter lasers. The resolver\'s hide-threshold was never told the same thing. `computeWeaponsToShow` multiplies the threshold by the number of copies only when the datasheet splits the swap into N independent groups (Talos, Carnifex Brood) or when the header says "one"/"the other"/"a" — neither matches "each Scatter laser" — so the threshold stayed at item.size, one swap reached it, and both lasers vanished from the profile and the printout. The same `each <weapon>` signal UnitCard reads is now read here too, kept as a separate condition from the "one" wording because they mean different things and only happen to need the same threshold. Verified end to end: no swap shows one Scatter laser row, swapping one shows Scatter laser and Shuriken cannon together, swapping both drops the laser.',
