    description: 'Most archetype restrictions are generic structural fields read by validators.ts/SlotPanel.tsx for every faction (see ki-40a). All 5 itemized gaps now fixed: IG Mechanised Company\'s "may only take a single Heavy Support selection" (`ArchetypeRule.slotCapOverride`, a flat cap below the AOP max). AdMech Cybernetica Cohort/Ordo Reductor Covenant\'s "must take at least one Magos/Archmagos with the Datasmith/Myrmidax upgrade" (`requiresHqUpgrade`, checks the HQ unit\'s own option_groups choice — or, for Tau Stealth Cadre below, an Armory item — not just the unit\'s name). AdMech Servitors\' own "for each Magos/Archmagos/Tech-Priest, one Servitor squad doesn\'t occupy an Elite slot" (a real datasheet ability sitting as an inert empty-choices option_group — `computeServitorFreeSlots`, same shape as Crusaders/Geminae Superia, which also got backfilled into SlotPanel.tsx\'s slot-full display while in there). IG Whiteshields\' "only one other Troop selection per Conscript Infantry Platoon" (`troopsRatioCap` — 0 anchor units means 0 others allowed at all, stricter than `slotCapOverride`). Sororitas Penitent Crusade ("for every 10 Arco-flagellant MODELS, one Penitent Engines may also count as Troops") and Tau Stealth Cadre ("for every 6 Stealth Shas\'ui/Shas\'vre MODELS, one Ghostkeel Battlesuits may also count as Troops" + "must include a Commander with an XV22 Stalker battlesuit") — both ratios are by MODEL COUNT not unit count, so a new `troopsModelRatioCap` field was needed (troopsRemap already let the capped unit count as Troops unconditionally; this adds the ratio ceiling as a validator error on top, rather than dynamically un-remapping individual entries). Votann Hearthfyre Arsenal\'s "for every 500pts of game size, one Brôkhyr Iron-master is free of its HQ slot" (new generic `pointsBasedHqFree` field + `computeArchetypeHqFreeSlots`, the archetype-rule equivalent of the existing per-unit `computeEldarWarlockFreeSlots` pattern) + "Hearthkyn Warriors do not count towards the 25% Troops requirement" (new `troopsCountExclude` field — an EXCLUSION list, the inverse of `troopsCount: \'remap\'`\'s INCLUSION-only list). FOLLOW-UP 2026-06-26: AdMech Servitor Maniple\'s own "for each Servitor unit taken as Troops, the army must also take a Tech-priest" requirement (distinct from Servitors\' universal free-Elite-slot ability, already fixed separately) was still unenforced — added `requiresEscortPerTroopsUnit` ({troopsUnit, escortUnit}), errors if Servitor-Troops count exceeds Tech-Priest count. The text\'s extra clause "this Tech-priest...must always be attached to a Servitor unit" (a join/attach-target constraint) is NOT enforced — would need the join system extended to validate WHICH unit a character is attached to, not just whether one is present; left as a minor open nuance, not blocking.',
